{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nProf. Vasechkin wants to represent positive integer n as a sum of addends, where each addends is an integer number containing only 1s. For example, he can represent 121 as 121=111+11+\u20131. Help him to find the least number of digits 1 in such sum.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++ code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nusing ll = long long;\nconst ll INF = 1e18;\nll ans = 0;\nvector<ll> dpr;\n\nll solve(ll n) {\n    if (n == 0) return 0;\n    if (n < (ll)dpr.size() && dpr[n]) return dpr[n];\n    \n    ll lastdif = INF;\n    ll x = 1;\n    ll i = 0;\n    \n    while (abs(x - n) <= lastdif) {\n        lastdif = abs(x - n);\n        x = x * 10 + 1;\n        i++;\n    }\n    \n    x /= 10;\n    \n    if (x > n && x / 10) {\n        ll option1 = i + solve(abs(x - n));\n        ll option2 = (i - 1) + solve(abs(x / 10 - n));\n        if (n < (ll)dpr.size()) return dpr[n] = min(option1, option2);\n        return min(option1, option2);\n    }\n    \n    ll result = i + solve(abs(x - n));\n    if (n < (ll)dpr.size()) return dpr[n] = result;\n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n#ifdef NEKROLM\n    freopen(\"input.txt\", \"r\", stdin);\n    freopen(\"output.txt\", \"w\", stdout);\n#endif\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    ll n;\n    cin >> n;\n    dpr.resize(100000000, 0);\n    cout << solve(n);\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nusing ll = long long;\n\nconst ll INF = 1e18;\nunordered_map<ll, ll> dp;\n\nll solve(ll n) {\n    if (n == 0) return 0;\n    if (n < 0) n = -n;\n    if (dp.find(n) != dp.end()) return dp[n];\n    \n    if (n < 10) {\n        return dp[n] = n;\n    }\n    \n    // Build the largest number with all 1s that is <= n\n    ll x = 1;\n    ll digits = 1;\n    while (x * 10 + 1 <= n) {\n        x = x * 10 + 1;\n        digits++;\n    }\n    \n    // Option 1: use x (the largest all-1s number <= n)\n    ll option1 = digits + solve(n - x);\n    \n    // Option 2: use the next larger all-1s number (if it's not too far)\n    ll next_x = x * 10 + 1;\n    if (next_x <= 2 * n) { // only consider if next_x is not too much larger than n\n        ll option2 = (digits + 1) + solve(next_x - n);\n        return dp[n] = min(option1, option2);\n    }\n    \n    return dp[n] = option1;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    ll n;\n    cin >> n;\n    \n    cout << solve(n);\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00021765247220173478, -2.264974000354414e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.125868119648658e-05, -2.50339189733495e-06, -8.22540732769994e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.2278481335670222e-05, -5.960446742392378e-06, -2.38418306253